{"created": "2026-10-16T12:27:26.138934+00:00", "modified": "2026-10-16T12:27:27.010990+00:00", "id": 23417397, "conceptrecid": "23417396", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23417397", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.23417396", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23417397", "metadata": {"title": "Theory of Everything Research Programme: Post-Block-V Revised Architecture.", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23417397", "publication_date": "2026-10-16", "description": "<p>This programme-level report records the revised Theory of Everything Research Programme architecture following completion of Experimental Blocks I&ndash;V and publication of the synthesis paper <em>From Candidate Hierarchy to Experimental Dependency Map</em>.</p>\n<p>The revision replaces the provisional sequential hierarchy with a typed, revisable dependency network comprising framework conditions, enabling conditions, scoped effective mechanisms, unresolved transition problems, documented bypass routes and an independent open problem concerning phenomenal consciousness.</p>\n<p>The revision retains FC1 as a framework condition, EC1 as a scoped enabling condition, and EM1&ndash;EM4 as scoped effective mechanisms. TP1 and TP2 remain open. TP3 and TP4 are experimentally narrowed but not closed. OP1 remains open and independent. Stronger claims concerning reciprocal maintenance necessity, universal world-model necessity and endogenous self-model necessity are reduced in light of the completed confirmatory evidence.</p>\n<p>This document introduces no new experimental data. It is an evidence-driven architectural revision derived from the completed preregistered Blocks I&ndash;V and the synthesis/results paper DOI <code>10.5281/zenodo.23413881</code>.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Craggs, Kenneth", "affiliation": "Independent Researcher", "orcid": "0009-0003-2075-3771"}], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.23413881", "relation": "isDerivedFrom", "resource_type": "publication", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.22857131", "relation": "isSupplementTo", "resource_type": "publication-workingpaper", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.22857179", "relation": "isSupplementTo", "resource_type": "publication-workingpaper", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.22857230", "relation": "isSupplementTo", "resource_type": "publication-workingpaper", "scheme": "doi"}], "resource_type": {"title": "Report", "type": "publication", "subtype": "report"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "23417396"}}]}}, "title": "Theory of Everything Research Programme: Post-Block-V Revised Architecture.", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23417397", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23417397", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23417397?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23417397", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23417397", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23417397", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23417397/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23417396", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23417396", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23417396", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23417396", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23417397/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23417397/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23417397/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23417397/media-files", "thumbnails": {"10": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23417397:POST_BLOCK_V_REVISED_TOE_ARCHITECTURE.pdf/full/%5E10,/0/default.jpg", "50": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23417397:POST_BLOCK_V_REVISED_TOE_ARCHITECTURE.pdf/full/%5E50,/0/default.jpg", "100": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23417397:P